From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_OVN_ROUTER_WARM warms the router kernels at boot

ai-engine e3492ca82 grafted onto the pin stack. A new module (cuda_router_warm.zig,
156 lines) warms the router kernels at boot (at level 2 the prompt-path mixer too),
taking the first layer of each kind as production's warm_routers does, and the engine
calls it after the weights load and before the server accepts requests. Knob off: warm
returns 0, no launches.

Pin adaptations (the source assumed the later era): moe.route does not exist at the pin,
so the warm's routed-expert call goes through moe.body (the router, top-k pick, plan
and experts, no fill); Forward.post's pin signature takes (rank, rows), so the warm's
call drops the two later args; the Forward literal drops split_min, which the pin lacks;
moeKernels and post are made pub for the warm module.

Gates on pin+0001..0014: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new.
